"""D9 - Print the concise ReAct versus plan-and-execute comparison."""
print("""ReAct uses 5 model calls for S1, 3 for S5 and 2 for S6 because it asks the model after each observation and once more for a final answer. Re-sending the growing history costs about 1,000 tokens for S1; a plan-and-execute design could ask for a step list once and use roughly two calls on a clean case. ReAct can stop when an observation says an order is missing or cancelled, while a fixed plan needs code guards or another model call to avoid inappropriate later steps. I would choose ReAct for refunds because each money-moving action depends on the previous database and policy results; the extra calls are bounded by the iteration, token and time limits and checkpoints.""")
